JCmodel -- the model corresponding to the Jukes Cantor model
************************************************************

Description
===========

The Jukes-Cantor (JK) Model is a Markov model of base substitution. It assumes
the root distribution vectors describe all bases occurring uniformly in the
ancestral sequence. It also assumes that the rate of all specific base changes
is the same. Thus the rates of bases changes A-G, A-T and A-C are the same.

The transition matrix has the form $$\begin{pmatrix} \alpha&\beta&\beta&\beta\\
\beta&\alpha&\beta&\beta\\ \beta&\beta&\alpha&\beta\\ \beta&\beta&\beta&\alpha
\end{pmatrix}$$

See also
========

  * *note Model: Model, -- a group-based model
  * *note CFNmodel: CFNmodel, -- the model corresponding to the
    Cavender-Farris-Neyman model or binary Jukes Cantor
  * *note K2Pmodel: K2Pmodel, -- the model corresponding to the Kimura
    2-parameter model
  * *note K3Pmodel: K3Pmodel, -- the model corresponding to the Kimura
    3-parameter model

For the programmer
==================

The object *note JCmodel: JCmodel, is an instance of the type *note Model:
Model,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

