joinIdeal -- compute the join of several ideals
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        joinIdeal(I,J)
        joinIdeal L
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of ideals in the same ring
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * DegreeLimit => ..., default value {}
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the join of the input ideals

Description
===========

This function computes the ideal of the join by constructing the abstract join
and then projecting with elimination.

Setting the optional argument *note DegreeLimit: (Macaulay2Doc)DegreeLimit, to
\{d\}  will produce only the generators of the join ideal up to degree d.

This method is general and will work for arbitrary polynomial ideals, not just
phylogenetic ideals.

+----------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d]        |
|                            |
|o1 = R                      |
|                            |
|o1 : PolynomialRing         |
+----------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal {a-d,b^2-c*d}|
|                            |
|                    2       |
|o2 = ideal (a - d, b  - c*d)|
|                            |
|o2 : Ideal of R             |
+----------------------------+
|i3 : J = ideal {a,b,c}      |
|                            |
|o3 = ideal (a, b, c)        |
|                            |
|o3 : Ideal of R             |
+----------------------------+
|i4 : joinIdeal(I,J)         |
|                            |
|            2               |
|o4 = ideal(b  - a*c)        |
|                            |
|o4 : Ideal of R             |
+----------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note secant: secant, -- compute the secant of an ideal

