leafTree -- construct a LeafTree
********************************

  * Usage: 
        leafTree(n,E)
        leafTree(L,E)
        leafTree(G)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of leaves
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of leaves
      * E, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of lists or sets specifying the
        internal edges
      * G, a *note graph: (Graphs)Graph,, a tree
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note LeafTree: LeafTree,, 

Description
===========

An object of class *note LeafTree: LeafTree, is specified by listing its
leaves, and for each internal edge, the partition the edge induces on the set
of leaves. L is the set of leaves, or if an integer n is input then the leaves
will be named $0,\ldots,n-1$. E is a list with one entry for each internal
edge. Each entry is a partition specified as a list or set of the leaves in one
side of the partition. Thus each edge can be specified in two possible ways.

An object of class *note LeafTree: LeafTree, can also be constructed from a
*note Graph: (Graphs)Graph, provided the graph has no cycles.

Here we construct the quartet tree, which is the tree with 4 leaves and one
internal edge.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = leafTree({a,b,c,d},{{a,b}})                                 |
|                                                                     |
|o1 = {{a, b, c, d}, {set {a, b}, set {a}, set {b}, set {c}, set {d}}}|
|                                                                     |
|o1 : LeafTree                                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : leaves T                                                        |
|                                                                     |
|o2 = set {c, d, a, b}                                                |
|                                                                     |
|o2 : Set                                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : edges T                                                         |
|                                                                     |
|o3 = {set {a, b}, set {a}, set {b}, set {c}, set {d}}                |
|                                                                     |
|o3 : List                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

Here is a tree with 5 leaves given as a *note Graph: (Graphs)Graph,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : G = graph{{a,b},{c,b},{b,d},{d,e},{d,f},{f,g},{f,h}}                    |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = Graph{a => {b}      }                                                   |
|           b => {a, c, d}                                                    |
|           c => {b}                                                          |
|           d => {b, e, f}                                                    |
|           e => {d}                                                          |
|           f => {d, g, h}                                                    |
|           g => {f}                                                          |
|           h => {f}                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Graph                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : T = leafTree G                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {{a, c, e, g, h}, {set {c, a}, set {c, e, a}, set {a}, set {c}, set {e},|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     set {g}, set {h}}}                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : LeafTree                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : leaves T                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = set {c, e, g, h, a}                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : Set                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : internalEdges T                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = {set {c, a}, set {c, e, a}}                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

