phyloToricLinears -- compute the linear invariants of a group-based phylogenetic model
**************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        phyloToricLinears(T,M)
        phyloToricLinears(n,E,M)
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note LeafTree: LeafTree,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of leaves
      * E, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the internal edges of the tree,
        given by one part of the bipartition on leaves
      * M, an instance of the type *note Model: Model,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note QRing: QRing, => ..., default value null, optional argument to
        specify Fourier coordinate ring
      * Random => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a generating set of the linear
        invariants

Description
===========

For models such as Jukes-Cantor (*note JCmodel: JCmodel,) and Kimura
2-parameter (*note K2Pmodel: K2Pmodel,), multiple variables in the Fourier
coordinates may map to the same monomial under the monomial map that defines
the toric variety of the model.  These equivalencies give rise to linear
relations in the space of Fourier coordinates.

The number of linear invariants is the codimension of the smallest linear
subspace in which the toric variety of the model is contained.

The optional argument *note QRing: QRing, can be passed the ring of Fourier
coordinates.  Otherwise the function will create a new ring.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = leafTree(3,{})                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = {{0, 1, 2}, {set {0}, set {1}, set {2}}}                                |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : LeafTree                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = qRing(T, K2Pmodel)                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = S                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : phyloToricLinears(T, K2Pmodel, QRing=>S)                                |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {q      - q     , q      - q     , q      - q     , q      - q     ,    |
|       1,2,3    1,3,2   2,1,3    3,1,2   2,3,1    3,2,1   2,2,0    3,3,0     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     q      - q     , q      - q     }                                       |
|      2,0,2    3,0,3   0,2,2    0,3,3                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note phyloToricFP: phyloToricFP, -- compute the invariants of a
    group-based phylogenetic model with toric fiber products
  * *note phyloToric42: phyloToric42, -- compute the invariants of a
    group-based phylogenetic model with 4ti2
  * *note phyloToricQuads: phyloToricQuads, -- compute the quadratic invariants
    of a group-based phylogenetic model

