secant -- compute the secant of an ideal
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        secant(I,n)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, order of the secant
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * DegreeLimit => ..., default value {}
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the kth secant of I

Description
===========

This function computes the kth secant of I by constructing the abstract secant
and then projecting with elimination.

Here the kth secant means the join of k copies of I. Setting k to 1 gives the
dimension of the ideal, while 2 is the usual secant, and higher values
correspond to higher order secants.

Setting the optional argument *note DegreeLimit: (Macaulay2Doc)DegreeLimit, to
\{d\}  will produce only the generators of the secant ideal up to degree d.

This method is general and will work for arbitrary polynomial ideals, not just
phylogenetic ideals.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d]                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal {a^2-b,a^3-c,a^4-d}                                           |
|                                                                             |
|             2       3       4                                               |
|o2 = ideal (a  - b, a  - c, a  - d)                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : secant(I,2)                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|             3             2      2            2    2                2     2 |
|o3 = ideal (b  - 2a*b*c + a d + 2c  - 2b*d, a*b  - a c - b*c + a*d, a b - b  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                   3                                                         |
|     - 2a*c + 2d, a  - 3a*b + 2c)                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note joinIdeal: joinIdeal, -- compute the join of several ideals

Ways to use secant:
===================

  * "secant(Ideal,ZZ)"

