toricJoinDim -- dimension of a join of toric varieties
******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        toricJoinDim(A,B)
        toricJoinDim L
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the A-matrix of a toric
        variety
      * B, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the A-matrix of a toric
        variety
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of A-matrices of toric varieties
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the dimension of the join of the
        toric varieties defined by the matrices

Description
===========

A randomized algorithm for computing the affine dimension of a join of toric
varieties using Terracini's Lemma.

Each input matrix defines a parameterization of the variety.  For each variety,
a vector of parameter values is chosen at random from a large finite field.
The dimension of the sum of the tangent spaces at those points is computed.

This algorithm is much much faster than computing the join variety.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = matrix{{4,3,2,1,0},{0,1,2,3,4}}|
|                                        |
|o1 = | 4 3 2 1 0 |                      |
|     | 0 1 2 3 4 |                      |
|                                        |
|              2       5                 |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : B = matrix{{1,1,1,1,1}}            |
|                                        |
|o2 = | 1 1 1 1 1 |                      |
|                                        |
|              1       5                 |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : toricJoinDim(A,B)                  |
|                                        |
|o3 = 3                                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : toricJoinDim(B,B)                  |
|                                        |
|o4 = 1                                  |
+----------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

All input matrices must have the same number of columns.

See also
========

  * *note toricSecantDim: toricSecantDim, -- dimension of a secant of a toric
    variety
  * *note joinIdeal: joinIdeal, -- compute the join of several ideals

Ways to use toricJoinDim:
=========================

  * "toricJoinDim(List)"
  * "toricJoinDim(Matrix,Matrix)"

